    {
      "text": "Herod will seek the young child to destroy him, Matt. 2:13. Think not that I am come to destroy the law, Matt. 5:17. fear him which is able to destroy both soul and body, Matt. 10:28. held a council … how they might destroy him, Matt. 12:14 (Mark 3:6; 11:18; Luke 19:47). destroy those wicked men, Matt. 21:41 (Mark 12:9; Luke 20:16). I am able to destroy the temple of God, Matt. 26:61 (Mark 14:58). persuaded the multitude that they should ask Barabbas, and destroy Jesus, Matt. 27:20. Thou that destroyest the temple, Matt. 27:40 (Mark 15:29). art thou come to destroy us, Mark 1:24 (Luke 4:34). Son of man is not come to destroy men’s lives, Luke 9:56. Destroy this temple, and in three days, John 2:19. will not hear that prophet, shall be destroyed, Acts 3:23. Is not this he that destroyed them which called, Acts 9:21. destroy the wisdom of the wise, 1 Cor. 1:19. defile the temple of God, him shall God destroy, 1 Cor. 3:17. belly for meats: but God shall destroy both, 1 Cor. 6:13. destroyed of serpents, 1 Cor. 10:9. destroyed of the destroyer, 1 Cor. 10:10. cast down, but not destroyed, 2 Cor. 4:9. now preacheth the faith which once he destroyed, Gal. 1:23 (2:18). through death he might destroy him, Heb. 2:14. lawgiver, who is able to save and to destroy, James 4:12. that he might destroy the works of the devil, 1 Jn. 3:8. destroyed them that believed not, Jude 1:5. destroy them which destroy the earth, Rev. 11:18.",
